WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.862
When Fraulein left Heidi's room, Heidi broke into a wild fit of weeping.

2
00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:20.304
"Now Grannie's rolls are all gone!"

3
00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:21.564
she cried.

4
00:00:21.584 --> 00:00:26.766
"They were all for Grannie and now they are all gone!"

5
00:00:28.347 --> 00:00:30.528
Clara was distressed at Heidi's tears.

6
00:00:31.444 --> 00:00:34.285
"Heidi, Heidi, please don't cry!"

7
00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:35.825
she said desperately.

8
00:00:35.845 --> 00:00:41.467
"I promise that when you go home, you shall have as many fresh rolls for Grannie as you

9
00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:44.748
want. Yours would have been hard and dry by then.

10
00:00:45.508 --> 00:00:47.688
Please, Heidi, don't cry anymore."

11
00:00:48.909 --> 00:00:54.250
Clara's promise comforted Heidi a little, but she did not stop sobbing for a long time.

12
00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.671
When she arrived at supper, her eyes were still red from crying.

13
00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:03.469
She sat quietly at the table and tried her best to be well behaved.

14
00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:10.133
Whenever Sebastian caught her eye, he pointed strangely to his head and then to hers.

15
00:01:10.853 --> 00:01:13.555
Heidi couldn't understand what he was trying to tell her.

16
00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:19.118
But when she went to bed that night, she found her old straw hat under her bedspread.

17
00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:23.981
She snatched it up with delight and hugged it.

18
00:01:24.541 --> 00:01:29.724
Then she wrapped a handkerchief around it and hid it as far back in her cupboard as she

19
00:01:29.784 --> 00:01:36.510
could. A few mornings later, there was a great commotion and much running up and down the stairs

20
00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:37.770
in the large house.

21
00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:45.272
Clara's father had just returned with packages and boxes and lots of pretty things.

22
00:01:46.032 --> 00:01:49.133
When he arrived, he immediately went to see Clara.

23
00:01:49.793 --> 00:01:52.014
Heidi was sitting beside her in the study.

24
00:01:52.574 --> 00:01:55.895
Father and daughter hugged each other with warm affection.

25
00:01:57.075 --> 00:02:03.393
Then, Herr Sesemann held out his hand to Heidi and said kindly, "So this is our little Swiss

26
00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:05.454
girl. Come and shake hands with me!

27
00:02:06.135 --> 00:02:08.576
Now tell me, are Clara and you good friends?"

28
00:02:09.416 --> 00:02:13.017
"Yes, Clara is very kind to me," answered Heidi.

29
00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:18.280
He stayed and talked with the girls for a few minutes, and then they left to eat supper.

30
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.702
Fraulein sat across from him at the table, her face sour with bad news.

31
00:02:23.722 --> 00:02:30.989
"Herr Sesemann, if you only knew the things Heidi has done─or the people and animals she has brought

32
00:02:31.029 --> 00:02:31.929
into this house!

33
00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.871
Her behavior is past understanding!"

34
00:02:35.891 --> 00:02:39.653
Clara's father listened to Fraulein, and he spoke with the tutor as well.

35
00:02:40.233 --> 00:02:41.534
Finally, he went to Clara.

36
00:02:41.554 --> 00:02:48.397
"And now, my dear little Clara," he said, pulling up his chair and taking her hand in his.

37
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:52.118
"What kind of animals has Heidi brought into the house?

38
00:02:52.718 --> 00:02:55.900
And why does Fraulein think that she is not in her right mind?"

39
00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.121
Clara had no difficulty explaining.

40
00:02:59.761 --> 00:03:02.862
She told her father about the kittens and the organ boy.

41
00:03:03.543 --> 00:03:08.665
Herr Sesemann laughed heartily and asked, "So do you want me to send Heidi home?"

42
00:03:08.685 --> 00:03:10.425
"Oh, no, no!"

43
00:03:11.106 --> 00:03:11.986
Clara exclaimed.

44
00:03:12.006 --> 00:03:14.247
"Please do not send her away."

45
00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:17.108
"It is settled then," said her father.

46
00:03:18.429 --> 00:03:21.030
Herr Sesemann was only home for a short time.

47
00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:27.744
He comforted Clara with the promise that Clara's Grandmamma would arrive soon to keep her company.

48
00:03:28.385 --> 00:03:31.966
Clara was overjoyed, and she told Heidi all about her.

49
00:03:33.147 --> 00:03:38.769
Upon her arrival, Clara's Grandmamma was eager to meet Heidi and welcomed her warmly.

50
00:03:39.349 --> 00:03:45.071
When Clara took her nap that afternoon, Grandmamma asked Fraulein, "Where is Heidi?

51
00:03:45.612 --> 00:03:47.752
And what does she do in the afternoons?"

52
00:03:47.772 --> 00:03:52.714
"She is sitting in her room, Frau Sesemann," said Fraulein.

53
00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:56.436
"Bring her to my room," said Grandmamma cheerfully.

54
00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:00.115
"I have some pretty books with me that I would like to give her."
